  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Physical Description
    
    A short-hafted blade of volcanic glass and shadow-steel, forged by Augur ☽'Milucaum~ Shadow-bane, a Nightshelf artificer, during the Orca Incursion. The blade's surface ripples like deep water under light that is not present. Its edge holds no reflection; illumination approaches and stops, as though the blade occupies a moment before light arrives. The grip is wrapped in cavern-fungus leather that retains faint warmth — attributed not to any thermal source but to the hands that last held it. Its weight never registers the same twice; those who hold it even briefly report phantom memory of cuts they never received.
    
    A notch near the crossguard marks where the blade met orca-bone during the Mbra∴silentiu, a battle of the Orca Incursion. Augur never had it sharpened out.
    
    ## Properties
    
    The blade channels Hush☽ Twilight, a Nightshelf suppressive technique derived from ☽Silv-glaciere☽ Arts that targets aurora-light itself. The suppression is structural — forged into the shadow-steel rather than applied by the wielder. Wounds inflicted do not bleed so much as *exhale*. The injured cease speaking of their pain, cease crying out, cease requesting aid — not from numbness but from suppression of the communicative impulse itself. Blood from its cuts strikes stone without sound. The blade has tasted orca-blood and penguin-blood in equal measure, per the canonical record.
    
    Drawing the blade extinguishes all light sources within approximately thirty body-lengths — fire-cores, bioluminescent fungi, everything — as though the blade inhales the photons. It responds to Hush☽ Twilight even when sheathed, growing visibly darker when the technique manifests nearby. It is drawn toward crystallized fissures left by the Pta∴extinct, pulling at the wielder's wrist with directional hunger aimed at whatever pulses in the deep below. When its edge meets Pta∴extinct crystal, the material exhales rather than shatters. After use, the blade sits warmer in its sheath than it should.
    
    The forging process itself imparted knowledge to Augur — forge-patterns and deep-pressure techniques that settled into their scarred hands as understanding too dangerous to share and too necessary to destroy.
    
    ## Service History
    
    Augur carried the blade through the darkening that extinguished aurora-light over the Twilight Shelf for seventeen days, collapsing trade and straining the Flipper Accord nearly to breaking. Augur emerged alone. The blade emerged darker.
    
    During subsequent tunnel-clearing operations beneath Sleek☽ Caemomot, a Nightshelf settlement, Augur was documented speaking to the blade on seventeen occasions while cutting through crystallized corruption barriers to maintain fire-core supply routes as the western shelf collapsed. Transcription efforts recovered no words. Three independent witnesses corroborated these observations; two later reported difficulty remembering the incidents at all.
    
    Augur was dispersed during the forbidden blood-working at Terrace Momiou. The blade survived its wielder.
    
    ## Classification and Current Status
    
    Nightshelf analysts have classified Veil☽ Sasvaeumis~ as having crossed from tool to *interlocutor* — an entity that listens and is spoken to. The Office of Deep-Archive Provenance contests this designation. Behavioral observation supports it. The Nightshelf Provenance Register (Vol. 65), compiled by Keeper-Registrar ☽'noctmuluevus 'born, catalogues the blade among three Incursion-damaged artifacts exhibiting irreversible change, noting a pattern of harm tied to bone-spiral frequencies.
    
    The blade is enshrined in Echo∴eliquiae, the Nightshelf memorial rule binding the living to carry forward the deeds of the fallen. It is bound under Pactum∴silenti: it cannot leave the deep, cannot be gifted, cannot be stolen without breaking covenant. It is additionally central to the Pactum∴ne accord, Lex∴andatum, Signum∴men, and The Way∴al — a density of legal binding unusual even for Nightshelf artifacts of this prominence.
    
    Those who carried it longest spoke to it in darkness, as if it listened. The record does not confirm that it answered. The record does not deny it.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771587160360_0", anchor: "speaking to the blade on seventeen occasions", text: "The Darkening lasted seventeen days. Augur spoke to the blade seventeen times. Either the Nightshelf transcribers were counting something real or they were rhyming — seventeen marks the threshold between witness and participant in Nightshelf numerical symbolism. I note this without endorsing it.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771587160360_1", anchor: "orca-blood and penguin-blood in equal measure, per the canonical record", text: "\"Equal measure\" is a moral claim dressed as metallurgy. The Provenance Register lists engagements but not casualties attributable to the blade specifically. What the ice preserves from the Mbra∴silentiu corridor is pressure-song residue and blood-scatter consistent with close-quarters fighting on both sides of a territorial line that penguins crossed first. \"Equal measure\" would mean something different if we admitted that. I let the phrase stand in the main text because the canonical record uses it. The canonical record was written by the victors.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771587160360_2", anchor: "The Office of Deep-Archive Provenance contests this designation", text: "That office is a desk, a seal, and me. The \"contest\" was a single memorandum I filed after examining the blade's ice-impression layer, which records no emanation pattern consistent with sentience — only with sustained exposure to pressure-depth magic. The Nightshelf analysts responded with behavioral data I could not refute. The memorandum remains on file. I remain unconvinced. The blade remains in the deep. One of us will outlast the others.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771587160360_3", anchor: "Augur never had it sharpened out", text: "A blade forged to suppress every communicative impulse — pain, speech, the sound of blood hitting stone — and its maker preserved the one mark that says *something happened here*. A weapon that silences everything, scarred by its artificer's refusal to let one moment go quiet.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771587160360_4", anchor: "a density of legal binding unusual even for Nightshelf artifacts", text: "Six governing instruments. At least two overlap in jurisdiction, and The Way∴al's application here contradicts its stated scope as a knowledge-dissemination doctrine. One does not bind a weapon under a law designed to free information unless one considers the weapon itself a form of knowledge that must not flow freely. Remarkable how clearly the Nightshelf legislate the opposite of what they profess, and how neatly the codification betrays the fear.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
